Z||000016||Jimmy||09-17-2001||11:26 PM||||OK guys, still waiting for my buddy to send me the video!  He works the night shift so I really only see him on weekends.  I do have a vhs copy but it doesn't look as good.  I'll try and get a hold of him tonight.  I know he converted it to mpg format.<P>Tina I usually run my car without the fan, only when I idle for long periods of time do I run the fan.  My temp never gets over 180 degrees.  If I run the fan at all times it never even gets close to warming up.  I am running a restrictor plate BTW not a thermostat.  I heard this is OK on carb setups.  BTW my motor is less than 300hp so that makes a bit of a difference in temp between my V8 and yours!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  My only problem with my cooling system is the moroso adapter with fillneck, seems it lets a little coolant past the cap(16 lbs) into my overflow in the engine bay.  After 500 miles I need to put a couple quarts back into my cooling system or else I'll get hot.<P>Jim<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000017||Tina||09-18-2001||11:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Jimmy:<BR><B>OK guys, still waiting for my buddy to send me the video!<BR>Jim</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE> <P>Let us know when is ready to go  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Tina I usually run my car without the fan, only when I idle for long periods of time do I run the fan.  My temp never gets over 180 degrees<BR>Jim</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Pretty much same set up here, exept the fan goes non stop on mine.<BR>Temp range between 180 and 220 depending on how I drive  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>BTW What waterpump are you running?<P>Tina<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||Jimmy||09-19-2001||01:12 AM||||Guys I'm sorry about the delay but I haven't been able to get a hold of the guy who shot the video since Sunday!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  It may very well be late this week before I can send the video off to STETZ, GreenGT, or the like so that they can post it for all.  Like I said before I have a vhs copy but its kinda dark footage(lighting) to start with and the transfer to video wasn't great.<P>Tina I am running a CSI electric waterpump.  It runs coolest at idle speed(water flows fast compared to rpm at idle).  If I don't use my fan on the freeway, and I'm really cruising along 85mph or so, i just take the car out of gear(lower the rpm) and the wind will cool the motor from about 200 degrees to 140.  I only had to do this on hot days when I was still figuring my cooling system out.  I could let my car idle or run for hours on end on our hottest days this summer and it would never reach 180 degrees when I had the fan on.  I was very surprised and happy of course.  <P>Tina BTW, I still haven't seen your car  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> and would love to swing buy sometime and meet you guys.  Seems like evyone I know knows you and Eric or your car!  "Have you seen that silver Fiero with a V8? Damn that thing is loud!" I must hear that from somebody once a week.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>BTW, My girlfriend lives in Coon Rapids which is near you I think.<P>Jim||||reg||1
